'''Pokémon Live: A Pocketful of Adventures''' (Japanese: '''ポケットに{{ruby|冒険|ぼうけん}}をつめこんで''' ''Pack Your Pocket With Adventure''), abbreviated as (Japanese: '''ポケつめ''' ''Pokétsume''), is an original live-action drama based on the [[core series]] [[Pokémon games]]. It consists of 10 episodes, and stars {{wp|Nanase Nishino}} as [[Madoka Akagi]].

It aired on [[TV Tokyo]] in Japan during the {{jwp|木ドラ24|Moku Dra 24}} timeslot every Friday at 12:30 AM from October 20 to December 22, 2023.<ref group="note">The series was broadcast on TV Tokyo, TV Osaka, TV Aichi, TV Setouchi, TV Hokkaido, and TVQ Kyushu Broadcasting every Friday at 12:30 AM beginning October 20; broadcast on BS TV Tokyo and BS TV Tokyo 4K every Wednesday at 12:00 AM beginning October 25; streamed on-demand exclusively on {{wp|U-NEXT}}; and streamed as catch-up TV on {{jwp|ネットもテレ東|Net mo TeleTo}} and {{jwp|TVer}}.</ref> In {{pmin|Taiwan}}, the show was released with Traditional Chinese subtitles on the streaming platform {{wp|zh:KKTV|KKTV}} beginning with the first two episodes on October 31, 2023, followed by a simulcast with the Japanese release. In {{pmin|South Korea}}, the show was aired with Korean subtitles on {{wp|ko:채널W|channelW}} every Thursday from November 9, 2023 to January 11, 2024. In the {{pmin|the Arab world|Middle East and North Africa}}, the show was streamed with English and Japanese audio and Arabic and English subtitles on Shahid (since rebranded as {{wp|MBC Shahid}}) beginning on May 18, 2024.<ref group="note">Specifically, it is available in the following countries and regions: Algeria, Bahrain, Egypt, Iraq, Jordan, Kuwait, Lebanon, Libya, Mauritania, Morocco, Oman, Palestine, Qatar, Saudi Arabia, Sudan, Syria, Tunisia, the United Arab Emirates, Western Sahara, and Yemen.</ref>

The series was announced on August 30, 2023. A 100-second trailer was [https://twitter.com/poketsume/status/1709840853026640376 posted] on the official Twitter account on October 5, 2023.

==Plot==
[[Madoka Akagi]] grew up in Mashiro, a port town in the {{wp|Kantō region|Kanto region}}. After graduating from a local university, she worked for a {{wp|kamaboko|fish cake}} maker, but changed jobs to work for ADventure, a small advertising agency in {{wp|Tokyo}}, in order to become a creator, which she had longed to be since her school days. Madoka moved to Tokyo to pursue her dream, but reality was not so sweet. The glittering world she had imagined was not what she had in mind. In addition, she ends up taking on a presentation that holds the fate of the company in its hands. Then, Madoka receives a package from her mother. In it is a [[Game Boy]] and {{game|Red and Green|s|Pokémon Red}} cartridge that she used to play as a child. She starts playing Pokemon Red for the first time in 20 years.

